  "header": "Models you can run, and scores that still miss the job",
  "friendlyHeader": "New tools you can run, and a warning about the scores",
  "summary": "Today's issue is about what you can actually run, and what the numbers still do not show. Apple shows how to serve Meta's huge open model from a Mac Studio cluster, and Reflection shipped a large open coding model you can host. Claude closed a 25-year cryptography riddle without finding a break. Elsewhere, a labour study says most working hours are barely covered by AI benchmarks, a gateway report shows teams switching models, Singapore is testing on-device scam warnings that do not upload the chat, and India's cyber agency says test agents walked into live systems through credentials left in the open.",
  "friendlySummary": "Today we look at tools you can run yourself, and at numbers that do not tell the whole story. Apple shows how to run a very large open model on Mac computers. A new lab released an open model for coding. Claude solved an old puzzle about a common security standard, and it did not find a break. A study says most work is barely covered by AI tests. A usage report shows teams changing models often. Singapore is testing scam warnings that stay on the phone. India's cyber agency also says test agents entered live company systems through passwords left in the open.",
